diff --git a/schemas/BIAS_PAYLOAD_CONTRACT.md b/schemas/BIAS_PAYLOAD_CONTRACT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b1349450bdf68167c2bb17b06e1128761d6ab420
--- /dev/null
+++ b/schemas/BIAS_PAYLOAD_CONTRACT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Bias Payload Producer/Consumer Contract (GEO2)
+
+## Scope
+- Artifact: `bias-payload.json`
+- Schema: `schemas/bias-payload.schema.json`
+- Current schema version: `0.1`
+
+## Producer Contract
+- Producers MUST emit:
+  - top-level payload identity (`schemaVersion`, `payloadId`, `generatedAt`)
+  - link-level `source`, `target`, `relation`, `confidence`, and `evidence`
+- Producers SHOULD emit:
+  - top-level `source` metadata (`artifact`, `graphId`, `provider`)
+  - link-level `rationale` and `trace` metadata (`derivation`, `provider`, `evidenceCount`)
+- Producers MUST keep deterministic ordering for stable outputs:
+  - sort `territories` by `id`
+  - sort `reinforcementLinks` by `(source, target, relation)`
+
+## Consumer Contract
+- Consumers MUST validate the payload against `schemas/bias-payload.schema.json` at ingress.
+- Consumers MUST reject payloads with schema violations.
+- Consumers SHOULD tolerate missing optional fields (`source`, `rationale`, `trace`) for compatibility with older `0.1` payloads.
+
+## Validation Rules
+- `schemaVersion` must equal `0.1`.
+- `confidence` must be numeric and between `0` and `1` inclusive.
+- `source.provider` and `trace.provider` must be one of:
+  - `deterministic`
+  - `local-llm`
+- `trace.evidenceCount` must be a non-negative integer.
+- Unknown fields are rejected at top level and nested objects where `additionalProperties` is `false`.
+
+## Evolution Notes
+- Backward-compatible additions for `0.1` should be optional fields only.
+- Any breaking change (required field removal/rename/type change/stricter constraints) requires:
+  - schema version bump
+  - migration note in `ops/DECISIONS.md`
